---
import {launchBook,PUBLISHING_PATHS} from '../../lib/studio/publicationBook';
const {project}=Astro.props;
const initial={book:launchBook(project.settings??{}),updatedAt:project.updated_at,sources:[]};
---
<section data-chapter-panel="into-the-world" data-launch hidden class="chapter-launch">
<script type="application/json" data-launch-initial set:html={JSON.stringify(initial).replaceAll('<','\\u003c')}/>
<nav class="launch-moments" aria-label="Into the World moments">{['My success','The deck story','Publishing path','Release plan','Launch and handover','Life of the deck'].map((s,i)=><button type="button" data-launch-step={i}>{s}</button>)}</nav>
<div data-launch-panel="0"><p class="studio-eyebrow">Section eight · Into the World</p><h2>Where would you like your work to go?</h2><p>Sharing a few handmade copies, using a deck professionally and publishing for a wider audience can all be meaningful destinations. You define success; sales and follower counts are not a default measure.</p><label>What success means to me<textarea data-launch-field="success" rows="5"/></label><label>The people I hope to reach<textarea data-launch-field="audience" rows="3"/></label><button type="button" class="studio-button studio-button--secondary" data-chapter="spark">Revisit my Creative North Star</button></div>
<div data-launch-panel="1" hidden><p class="studio-eyebrow">Telling your deck's story</p><h2>Introduce the work in your own words.</h2><p>This draft stays private. Write below or choose saved excerpts; nothing is selected automatically.</p><label>Intended audience for this story draft<select data-launch-audience><option value="">Still deciding</option><option value="personal">People I choose personally</option><option value="professional">My professional audience</option><option value="public">A future public audience</option></select></label><p><strong>Still private:</strong> this choice records an intended audience. It does not share the draft with anyone.</p><details><summary>Choose words I have already prepared</summary><div data-launch-sources/><p>Journal options are existing prepared excerpts, not complete journal entries. Make or edit an excerpt using the existing <a href={`/studio/projects/${project.id}/crowd-funding/`}>journey update tool</a>; choosing one here still does not publish it.</p><label class="launch-check"><input type="checkbox" data-launch-approval/>I approve exactly the selected excerpts for this private story draft.</label><button type="button" class="studio-button studio-button--secondary" data-launch-prepare>Build a draft from my selected words</button><p>Selected words are joined without AI rewriting. You can edit the story independently. Existing text is replaced only after your confirmation.</p></details><div data-launch-source-review/><label>Short description<textarea data-launch-field="shortDescription" rows="3"/></label><label>My editable deck story<textarea data-launch-field="story" rows="8"/></label><details class="studio-local-recovery"><summary>Recover unsaved work</summary><p>Keep a local copy of current editor state. Normal saved outputs are in Exports.</p><button type="button" class="studio-button studio-button--secondary" data-launch-story-download>Recover this story draft</button></details></div>
<div data-launch-panel="2" hidden><p class="studio-eyebrow">Choosing a publishing path</p><h2>Choose a route that fits your intention.</h2><p>Paths can overlap. None requires a commercial launch or crowdfunding campaign.</p>{Object.entries(PUBLISHING_PATHS).map(([key,label])=><label class="launch-check"><input type="checkbox" data-launch-path={key}/>{label}</label>)}<details data-launch-crowdfunding><summary>Would crowdfunding serve this edition?</summary><p>Consider edition specifications, evidenced supplier costs, net funding needs after fees and fulfillment, feasible rewards, audience preparation and delivery obligations. Gross pledges are not profit.</p><label>Readiness evidence and questions<textarea data-launch-field="crowdfunding" rows="6"/></label><label>Live campaign duration (if considered)<input data-launch-campaign placeholder="Undecided — check the chosen provider's rules"/></label><p>This is separate from your communications lead-in. No crowdfunding account, campaign, rewards or payments are created.</p></details></div>
<div data-launch-panel="3" hidden><p class="studio-eyebrow">Preparing for release</p><h2>Give the introduction room to grow.</h2><p>A concentrated lead-in may help, but there is no universally optimal length. Choose a planning starting point, then adapt it to your readiness and commitments.</p><div class="launch-presets">{[5,7,9].map(n=><button type="button" class="studio-button studio-button--secondary" data-launch-weeks={n}>{n}-week lead-in</button>)}</div><label>My editable lead-in, in weeks<input type="number" min="1" max="104" data-launch-weeks-input placeholder="Undecided"/></label><p data-launch-timing/><label>Before release: materials, testing and truthful expectations<textarea data-launch-field="releaseBefore" rows="5"/></label><label>Rights, responsibilities and economic assumptions<textarea data-launch-field="rights" rows="4"/></label><p>Confirm the edition, permissions, delivered costs, channels and obligations yourself. This planner does not certify readiness.</p><button type="button" class="studio-button studio-button--secondary" data-chapter="making">Review my Production Book</button></div>
<div data-launch-panel="4" hidden><p class="studio-eyebrow">Launch and handover</p><h2>Introduce it in a way that feels right.</h2><p>A personal letter, workshop, exhibition or thoughtful article can be a launch. Keep promises proportionate to what you can deliver.</p><label>At release: what I will introduce and promise<textarea data-launch-field="releaseDuring" rows="5"/></label><label>After release: delivery, access and communication<textarea data-launch-field="releaseAfter" rows="5"/></label><p>Nothing on this page posts, sends announcements, opens orders, contacts recipients or handles their personal information.</p></div>
<div data-launch-panel="5" hidden><p class="studio-eyebrow">The life of your deck</p><h2>Celebrate, listen, preserve—or simply finish.</h2><label>Learning, corrections and possible future editions<textarea data-launch-field="learning" rows="5"/></label><p>You may continue developing the work, preserve it or stop. Finishing does not create an obligation to launch another project.</p><div data-launch-summary/><details class="studio-local-recovery"><summary>Recover unsaved work</summary><p>Keep a local copy of current editor state. Normal saved outputs are in Exports.</p><button type="button" class="studio-button studio-button--secondary" data-launch-book-download>Recover current Publication and Launch notes</button></details><p>This is a private planning export and may contain costs or working notes. Review it before sharing. This download contains the Publication and Launch Book. My Project Workbook brings together your saved Section outputs; nothing is published.</p></div>
<div class="launch-actions"><button type="button" class="studio-button studio-button--secondary" data-launch-save>Save my Publication Book</button><button type="button" class="studio-button" data-launch-next>Continue</button></div><p data-launch-status role="status" aria-live="polite">Private publication planning. Nothing has been published.</p>
</section>
<script>import '../../scripts/chapterPublication';</script>
<style>.chapter-launch h2{font:clamp(1.8rem,3vw,2.5rem)/1.2 'Playfair Display',Georgia,serif}.chapter-launch p{line-height:1.7}.launch-moments{display:flex;gap:.3rem;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:.83rem;margin-bottom:1rem}.launch-moments button{border:0;border-bottom:2px solid transparent;padding:.5rem .3rem;background:none;font:inherit;color:inherit;cursor:pointer}.launch-moments button[aria-current]{border-color:#8a6a1f;font-weight:600}.chapter-launch label{display:grid;gap:.5rem;margin:1.2rem 0;font-weight:600}.chapter-launch input,.chapter-launch textarea,.chapter-launch select{box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;padding:.75rem;font:400 1rem/1.6 Inter,system-ui,sans-serif;color:#242b2b;background:#fff;border:1px solid #9d9e94;border-radius:3px}.chapter-launch textarea{resize:vertical}.chapter-launch .launch-check{display:flex;align-items:start;gap:.65rem;font-weight:400}.chapter-launch .launch-check input{width:1.1rem;height:1.1rem;flex:none;margin-top:.25rem}.launch-image{display:block;width:100%;height:180px;object-fit:cover;margin:1rem 0 .4rem}.launch-credit{font-size:.72rem;color:#58605d}.launch-presets,.launch-actions{display:flex;gap:.65rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:1rem 0}.chapter-launch :global(.launch-source){border-bottom:1px solid #cec9c1;padding:.6rem 0}.chapter-launch :global(.launch-source label){display:flex;align-items:start;gap:.65rem}.chapter-launch :global(.launch-source input){width:1.1rem;height:1.1rem;flex:none}.chapter-launch :global(.launch-source p){white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font-weight:400}.chapter-launch :global(.launch-warning){border-left:3px solid #8a6a1f;padding-left:.75rem}.chapter-launch [hidden]{display:none!important}@media(max-width:760px){.launch-actions .studio-button{width:100%}.launch-image{height:160px}}</style>


